# WISEPACK machine-local settings — TEMPLATE. Safe to commit.
#
#     cp config/local.env.example config/local.env
#     # edit the placeholders below
#
# THIS FILE IS OPTIONAL.
#
# Nothing here is required to run WISEPACK, and nothing here decides whether
# WebRTC works. Every value can equally be exported inline:
#
#     WISEPACK_ISAAC_STREAM_HOST=<reachable-server-address> \
#     ./run_wisepack_dashboard.sh isaac
#
# The file exists only so host-specific values do not have to be retyped on
# every invocation. `config/local.env` is git-ignored on purpose: it describes
# THIS host and must not travel with the repository. Nothing in it is a secret
# in the cryptographic sense, but a published SSH port is free reconnaissance,
# so real values stay out of tracked files, README examples, test fixtures,
# generated artefacts and logs. It is never committed.
#
# Read by an ALLOWLIST PARSER, not by the shell: only the keys below are
# honoured, and the file is never sourced — a backtick in a value is data.
#
# Resolution order for every value:
#   1. an already-exported environment variable (an explicit override wins)
#   2. config/local.env
#   3. a safe default, or an explicit "unresolved" diagnostic

# The SSH port of THIS server, used to build port-forwarding examples for the
# Isaac Sim WebRTC stream.
#
# NO SAFE DEFAULT, and 22 is NOT assumed: a guessed port produces a forwarding
# command that looks right, runs without error and connects somewhere else or
# nowhere. Left unresolved and reported instead. When the launcher runs inside
# an SSH session it can also read the server-side port from $SSH_CONNECTION.
WISEPACK_SSH_PORT=YOUR_SSH_PORT

# The address a REMOTE NVIDIA Isaac Sim WebRTC Streaming Client should dial.
#
# This is the ADVERTISED endpoint, not a bind address: Kit listens on 0.0.0.0
# whatever this says, so setting it does not open anything and leaving it unset
# does not close anything. Access control is a firewall or SSH-forward decision.
#
# Safe default when unset: 127.0.0.1, and the dashboard then labels the endpoint
# "local/forwarded" and tells you to set this for a remote client.
WISEPACK_ISAAC_STREAM_HOST=YOUR_REACHABLE_SERVER_ADDRESS

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PHYSICAL PERCEPTION (optional). Unset == simulated perception, unchanged.
#
# A THIRD AXIS, independent of the dashboard data source and of the execution
# backend: `camera` changes where the OBJECT OBSERVATIONS come from and nothing
# else. See README §15a.
#
# The two lines an ordinary camera user needs:
#     WISEPACK_PERCEPTION_SOURCE=camera
#     WISEPACK_PERCEPTION_CAMERA=2
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# sim (default) | camera
# An unrecognised value is a start-up ERROR, never a silent fall back to `sim`.
#WISEPACK_PERCEPTION_SOURCE=camera

# The camera: a device index (2), a device path (/dev/video2) or a stream URL.
# NO /dev/videoX is hardcoded anywhere; this is the only place it is decided.
#WISEPACK_PERCEPTION_CAMERA=2

# WHICH perception method processes the frame. A SEPARATE axis from the source:
# `camera` says the observations are measured from a real frame, this says how.
# One provider exists today; the variable is here so a second one (YOLO/OBB,
# RGB-D pose, segmentation) is a configuration change, not a rename.
#WISEPACK_PERCEPTION_DETECTOR=fasterrcnn_bottle

# Where the WISEPACK perception service listens. It runs on the HOST — which
# owns the camera, the GPU and torch — and is the SINGLE OWNER of the camera.
# It speaks HTTP only: nothing on the host needs ROS 2, Vulcanexus or Fast DDS.
#WISEPACK_PERCEPTION_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:22101

# The interpreter that runs the perception service. Leave unset to use the
# current provider's own environment, resolved exactly as its run.sh does:
#     <WISEPACK_HARMONY_PATH>/../torch_venv/bin/python
# The service needs torch, torchvision, cv2, fastapi and uvicorn; the system
# python3 has none of them, and is deliberately NOT used as a fallback — that
# produced `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'uvicorn'` at demo time.
# A path set here that is not executable is an error, not a reason to search on.
#WISEPACK_PERCEPTION_PYTHON=/data/arise/harmony/torch_venv/bin/python

# Detector weights. Leave unset to use the documented search order:
#   1. this variable  2. /data/arise/models/best_model.pth
#   3. <provider checkout>/models/best_model.pth  4. absent, with a fetch command
#WISEPACK_PERCEPTION_MODEL_PATH=/data/arise/models/best_model.pth

# How long the launcher waits for the service's /health after starting it. The
# first request imports torch and loads a ~159 MB model, so this is generous by
# design — but bounded, so a hang is never an indefinite wait.
#WISEPACK_PERCEPTION_READY_TIMEOUT=180

# Where the launcher-owned perception service writes its log.
#WISEPACK_PERCEPTION_LOG=/tmp/wisepack_perception.log

# KNOWN dimensions of the physical proxy cylinders. A 2-D detector measures
# WHERE an object is, not how big it is, so the geometry the packer needs is
# declared rather than invented from a bounding box. MEASURE YOUR OBJECTS: the
# defaults describe an ordinary 0.5 l PET bottle.
#WISEPACK_PHYSICAL_PROXY_DIAMETER_MM=65
#WISEPACK_PHYSICAL_PROXY_LENGTH_MM=215

# --- settings specific to the current `fasterrcnn_bottle` provider ----------
# An ordinary camera user never needs these. They describe where that
# provider's checkout lives and how its ArUco calibration board is printed.
#WISEPACK_HARMONY_PATH=/data/arise/harmony/ai-bottle-detector-fiware
#WISEPACK_HARMONY_CORNER_MARKERS=11,10,15,16
#WISEPACK_HARMONY_CORNER_EXTENT_MM=130
#WISEPACK_PHYSICAL_WORKAREA_WIDTH_MM=130
#WISEPACK_PHYSICAL_WORKAREA_DEPTH_MM=130
